How {{PROJECT_NAME}} is built, validated, and kept current.

## The pipeline at a glance

One command, `uv run python -m scripts.pipeline run`, runs the stages in
order and stops at the first failure. Publishing is a separate step (and a
separate workflow), so a routine refresh never deploys without review.

```
discover → fetch → clean → audit → reconcile     (the `run` command)
                                       ↓
                                   publish       (separate: `pipeline publish`)
```

`clean` parses each original, removes duplicate keys, validates against the
schema, and sets rejected rows aside with a reason. It checks that every
parsed row was written, dropped as a duplicate or rejected, and fails the build
otherwise; it never writes an empty or partial table over a good one.

